+
+## Initial Codex model selection
+
+On Linux, an initial public start can select the exact model `gpt-6-astra`:
+
+```sh
+substrate agent start --backend cli:codex-host --model gpt-6-astra --prompt 'Review this workspace'
+substrate agent start --backend cli:codex-world --scope world --model gpt-6-astra --prompt 'Review this workspace'
+```
+
+World scope starts the configured host orchestrator. Its actual backend must also
+be Codex. Selection requires an already enabled world and an enabled `in_world`
+gateway; it never enables either setting. Other models, native backends, platforms
+and `host_only` gateway mode are rejected. Omitting `--model` retains the existing
+`codex` route to `codex-mini-latest`.
+
+The initial selection and managed gateway endpoint are bound to the authenticated
+original session. Continuation and fork inherit that wiring; they have no model
+switch option. A session keeps its private native home for its existing lifetime.
+Missing or substituted context or native home causes refusal before native launch.
+Child native configuration cannot replace the selected model, provider, endpoint
+or ephemeral credential-store setting. Account credentials stay with the gateway.
+Stock native capabilities and WebSocket-to-HTTP fallback remain available.
+
+Selected startup refuses unsupported administrative Codex configuration under
+`/etc/codex` and the presence (including empty values) of
+`OPENAI_FEDERATION_RULE_ID`, `OPENAI_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE` or
+`OPENAI_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_CONTEXT`. These workload-auth inputs cannot be safely
+removed through the existing per-launch wrapper environment map.
+
+A running Codex gateway cannot be reused for an explicit selection in this slice.
+A conflicting selection, an attempt to reset a selected runtime by omitting the
+option, or a recovered Codex runtime whose birth selection cannot be established
+is refused before recovery, restart or configuration rewrite. Existing runtime
+artifacts and processes are preserved on refusal. Non-Codex omitted lifecycle
+behavior is unchanged. The internal `SUBSTRATE_INITIAL_CODEX_MODEL` key is carried
+in the explicit lifecycle request environment; ambient process environment does
+not select a model.
